{"body":"Fixes #751. run_sweep only called first_run when it generated a missing config, so a config left enabled: false after a failed first run (for example worktree_invalid) was skipped as not_enabled forever. It now retries first_run for a disabled config whose first-run report says first-run: failed (config step every sweep, later steps after one hour; never on a dry run, on a config generated in the same sweep, or when the report is missing or says passed). Tests: 9 for failed_step and 7 retry tests (six fail against the old dispatch.py); tests/issue_watch passes (3030) and ruff is clean; the full repository suite was not run locally. Known limits: a crash between generating the config and its first run, or an unwritable report, still leaves no failed report, so those cases are not retried; the not_enabled skip text does not mention the one-hour delay. 🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOPOT5c88AAAABqSa2uA","author":{"login":"chatgpt-codex-connector"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"<!-- codex-pull-request-review-summary -->\n<!-- codex-review-state:v1 {\"code_review\":{\"commit_sha\":\"21dbd8883bbc37f93841dd85a92f9fdebd31912c\",\"has_any_findings\":false,\"has_unresolved_findings\":false,\"status\":\"completed\"},\"security_review\":{\"commit_sha\":\"21dbd8883bbc37f93841dd85a92f9fdebd31912c\",\"has_any_findings\":null,\"has_unresolved_findings\":null,\"status\":\"completed\"}} -->\n<!-- codex-security-review:v1 {\"blockingSeverityThreshold\":\"P0\",\"headSha\":\"21dbd8883bbc37f93841dd85a92f9fdebd31912c\",\"mergeGateEnabled\":false,\"pullRequestNumber\":759,\"repository\":\"IronbellyOrg/IronClaude\",\"status\":\"completed\"} -->\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Codex Review Summary</strong>: ✅ Completed</summary>\n\nThis comment shows the latest Codex review activity on this pull request.\n\n| Review | Status | Commit | Review trigger |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 📝 **Code Review** | ✅ **Completed** <rel